Z||000000||U Wanna Race||11-03-2001||03:46 AM||||I want to put a 10 or 12 inch sub behind the passenger seat.  I want to know exactly how much room there is from the carpeted backing to the firewall.  Unless someone knows of a better place to put a sub.  And the spare tire sub is out of the question.||||reg||5
Z||000001||grinthock||11-03-2001||08:30 AM||||Fiero has a double firewall, some people cut away the first firewall and use the inner side of the firewass as a baffle for a freeair sub, some pics are around of it and instructions if you look<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fieroworld.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fieroworld.com</A>  The place to go for Fiero INFO! <BR>Home of my 87 GT and 85 GT<BR>Justin C.<BR>Engineer, Designer and<BR>Technical Trainer for Nortel Networks Business Products.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||11-03-2001||08:47 AM||||I forget the dimensions, but you gain about 2 1/2" in depth.  Just about enough for the magnet.  Originally, I was going to go this route before deciding on a box in the front compartment.  I've got a pic of the cutout before I glassed it in.  You have to glass it in because the area isn't sealed from the outside.  I just cut a hole in the middle of the area and used a coat hanger to feel around to see where the edges were.  Then I used a jigsaw to cut it out.  Hammered the edges in so I wouldn't cut myself then fiberglassed the well.  The best info is on fierosounds website (can't find the URL right now).  He installed a sub on each side behind the seats.  Nice installation, too.  Here's the pic I have.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/firewall_cutout.JPG"> ||||reg||1
